                    <physDesc>
                        <objectDesc>
                            <supportDesc>
                                <support>
                                    <p>Two joining fragments preserving slightly less than one quarter of a small, probably locally produced, low hemispherical footless cup. The bowl is slightly deformed; it has an undifferentiated rounded rim, an externally concave base and a thin internal rib on the floor.</p>
                                    <material ana="#material.clay.fired" ref="https://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/material/lod/131.html">ceramic</material>
                                    <objectType ana="#object.vessel.cup" ref="http://kerameikos.org/id/cup">cup</objectType>
                                    <dimensions>
                                        <height unit="cm">2.4</height>
                                        <width unit="cm">6.2</width>
                                        <depth unit="cm"/>
                                        <dim type="diameter" subtype="rim" unit="cm">9</dim>
                                        <dim type="diameter" subtype="base" unit="cm">4.8</dim>
                                    </dimensions>
                                </support>
                                <condition ana="#condition.fragments.contiguous"/>
                            </supportDesc>
                            <layoutDesc>
                                <layout>
                                    <rs ana="#execution.painted" ref="https://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/writing/lod/10.html">painted</rs>
                                    <p>The inscription was painted before firing in a single line inside the bowl, approximately 1 cm below the rim, with a slight inclination following the curvature of the vessel. It was probably written from left to right. The inscription and decoration were painted with the same ochre pigment containing hematite.</p>
                                    <damage ana="#text_condition.incomplete #text_condition.legible"/>
                                </layout>
                            </layoutDesc>
                        </objectDesc>
                        <handDesc>
                            <handNote>
                                <p>The letters were painted with a fine brush, with a maximum stroke width of approximately 2-3 mm. Tau has an oblique upper stroke; alpha has a crossbar descending to the left and a short tail beyond the right stroke; iota is slightly curved to the left.</p>
                                <locus from="line1" to="line1">Line 1</locus>
                                <dimensions type="letterHeight">
                                    <height unit="mm">20-22</height>
                                </dimensions>
                            </handNote>
                        </handDesc>
                        <decoDesc>
                            <decoNote>Painted curved lines run from the rim on the exterior; an irregular sequence of painted dots appears inside the bowl above the inscription.</decoNote>
                        </decoDesc>
                    </physDesc>
